forward_once: before the drop, t is a backprop root and no longer a forward root: true
forward_once: the dropped graph is reclaimed: true
Train.forward: before the drop, t is a backprop root and no longer a forward root: true
Train.forward: the dropped graph is reclaimed: true
checkpoint: t is a backprop root when the checkpoint is taken: true
checkpoint: the dropped graph is reclaimed while the checkpoint is held: true
leg B: the held t is still a backprop root after collections: true
leg B: w.grad = 6 w: true
copy: the copy is a distinct record: true
copy: the copy is still a backprop root after collections: true
copy: w.grad = 6 w through the copy: true
trunk: before the drop, l1 is a backprop root and no longer a forward root: true
trunk: the dropped owner l1 is reclaimed: true
trunk: l2 is refused at run naming h's backprop fragment: true
restore: with_unchanged_roots puts the held root back: true
rewind: the consumer embedded t's backprop: true
rewind: the held root is a root again, its marker reset: true
rewind: an external handout stays excluded: true
consumer: the dropped consumer is reclaimed: true
consumer: its embedded child is neither root: true
consumer: consuming the child's forward code is still refused: true
closure: held by the last closure's checkpoint: true
closure: reclaimed once the next closure replaces the checkpoint: true
unevaluated: t is a forward and a backprop root: true
